## 6. Risks and required controls

| Risk | Control |
|---|---|
| Closing issues on a table rather than on evidence | UG1 makes every `met` an executable result; the owner closes (UG-D0) |
| A clean-today population is read as a durable guarantee | UG-R3; the contract text says the admitted constraint is `proposed`/`deontic` and advisory (§2.2) |
| Population bytes are untrusted | UG-R7: capped at the read, total over arbitrary JSON, time-bound test |
| A population for the wrong model or a stale one | UG-R5 digest binding; the check runs against the candidate model and refuses a population whose model digest does not match |
| The evolve lane gains a checker dependency | UG-Q1; the spec shows the lane map change with zero allowances or passes the verdict in through the command layer |
| `evolve/service.py` is 2221 lines | RF6 size and query ceilings measured in the UG2 spec; new logic lives beside `policy.py`, not in `service.py` |
| A new option moves RF1 goldens in unrelated commands | Only the two touched leaves are re-pinned; MG3-Q1 says a fresh RF1 capture drifts about 60 unrelated goldens, so each phase takes only its own |
| Disclosure leak through a violation message | UG-R6; a canary-value test |
| Drifting normative prose | UG-R4: one home; UG4 checks every other page cites |
| Declaring documents out of band is unaudited by `evolve` | UG-D9 is ruled (b), so UG3 (i) closes this; until it ships, UG1 pins the out-of-band step as an unaudited append-only header edit and shows a round passing only because of it; `gnd validate --document` still checks every cited span against the declared digest |
| A new locator widens the closed proposal contract | UG3 (i) spec states the schema-version decision (UG-Q5) and proves old proposals parse and digest unchanged (UG-R1) |
| Scope creep into the later wave | §7 |

## 7. Out of scope

- Issues 73, 77, 78, 95 (a later wave). Note for that wave: the model-growth-
  guardrails records say MG4 delivered extraction guidelines for issue 78, and
  issue 78 is still open. This milestone neither confirms nor dispositions it.
- Admitting `subtype_of`/`inherits_reference` on an existing object type under
  `--policy additive` (UG-D7 proposes to keep it a reviewed proposal).
- A shipped JSON Schema or translator for the host reply shape (UG-D5).
- Giving subtype links their own `status`/`modality` (a model-schema change,
  UG-D4).
- Any change to `gnd extract`, `gnd discover`, the discover fact-type judges or
  `gnd-model-from-text` Steps 1 to 7 as dialogue.
- Fixing MG3-Q2.
- Posting issue comments or closing issues without an explicit owner request.
- Certification or recertification (explicit owner request only); merge,
  release, publication.

## 8. Execution, approval and review protocol

`auto=false`. Each phase follows `process-phase`: spec, owner gate,
implementation with focused tests, one independent diff review, a refactoring
review, and a record. No code before recorded spec approval. UG1 changes no
source and still has its spec gate. Plan and close review: the project's bar is
the maintained panel (`project.md`); the predecessor ran four local readers by
owner ruling (UG-D1 asks again). Stop rule: at most one confirmation round after
round 1, restricted to blocking themes; stop early when most findings are
self-inflicted. Findings are unproved until reproduced. Work on topic branch
`claude/plan-unattended-model-growth-f116c3` for planning, then one branch per
implementation phase; PR each; merge on the owner's authorization only. Never
push to main.

## 9. Per-phase verification story

| Phase | Expected result | Focused gate (exact selection fixed in each spec) |
|---|---|---|
| UG1 | Replay and refusals pass; matrix complete; no source diff | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_unattended_model_growth_acceptance.py tests/test_unattended_mode.py tests/test_unattended_growth_guidance.py tests/test_evolve_additive_policy.py tests/test_evolve_shape_matches.py tests/test_growth_example.py --tb=short`; `uv run ruff check` on the new test |
| UG2 | As UG2-C1..C8 | UG1 gate plus `tests/test_rf1_cli_pins.py tests/test_disclosure_mode.py tests/test_rf1_layering.py tests/test_rf6_query_policy.py tests/test_gnd_arch.py` and a new `tests/test_evolve_population_check.py` — exact list unresolved until the spec |
| UG3 | As UG3-C1..C7 | `tests/test_unattended_mode.py`, RF1 pins, disclosure tests, a new case file — unresolved until the spec |
| UG4 | Pages executed, pins pass | `uv run python tools/run_tutorials.py`; `uv run --group docs zensical build --strict`; `uv run python tools/check_docs.py site`; `tests/test_packaged_skills.py` and the install/doctor/skill-census tests — exact list at spec time |

Affected consumers: anyone parsing the evolve preview JSON (additive keys only
under the new option); the RF1 goldens; the disclosure site table; the packaged
skill file inventory.

### Implementability sweep (author inspection, not review)

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| Can UG1 run today? | Yes: it uses only shipped commands; helpers exist in two test files; the planning-time run of the related tests was green (203 passed). |
| Does the evolve preview have a population to check? | No: `--policy` sees `--populated` ids, sample rows, reference populations and `population` artifact locators, never fact rows (`effective_populated`). UG2 adds the input; it cannot be a re-use. |
| Can the checker be run on a candidate model plus a population from the evolve lane? | Unresolved: `tools/gnd_layers.json` must be read for the lane edge (UG-Q1). Not asserted either way. |
| Is a falsifiable end-to-end result named for each promised capability? | 74/75/76: UG1-C1/C2. 104-5: UG2-C1/C2 or the UG-D2 (a) disposition. Span coverage: UG3-C2. |
| Can a document-by-document loop run through `evolve` today? | Only if each round's document is declared in the model file before the round (scratch probe, 2026-11-07, above). UG1 turns the probe into a test. |
| Can a host keep an admitted constraint `proposed`? | Yes for constraints; no for subtype links (UG-D4). |

## 10. Owner decisions and open questions

| ID | Question | Readings and cost | Proposal | Owner ruling |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| UG-D0 | Who closes issues 74, 75, 76 and 104 | (a) the owner, from drafted dispositions after merge; (b) an agent closes on the owner's explicit instruction per issue; an unprompted close is outward-facing and not reversible in effect | (a) | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "Approve all as proposed (Recommended)"** → (a). A decision ruling, not a plan-gate approval. |
| UG-D1 | Plan and close review instrument | (a) four local readers, as MG-D1/TS-D2 ruled; (b) the maintained six-seat panel, the project's stated bar, needs the parent credentials and costs more | (a), with the project's bar stated at the gate; the owner rules | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "Approve all as proposed (Recommended)"** → (a) four local readers, with the maintained panel stated as the project's bar. |
| UG-D2 | Issue 104 item 5, second option | (a) decline: keep "reviewed non-additive proposal" as the route and say so; no code, 104 closes on items 1 to 5-first-option; (b) build the population-checked admission (§2.2): a new option on two commands, a new input to digest-bind, a lane edge; unattended hosts finally have a route for late-discovered constraints; (c) a narrower build: admit only when the supplied population is the model's own declared reference population (no new input): smaller, but hosts keep extracted facts outside the model, so it would not help them | (b). It is the only reading that closes the hole the issue reports. Cost: UG2 | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "(b) Build it (Recommended)"** → UG2 is to be built; it is still subject to its own spec gate. |
| UG-D9 | How a growth round declares its document (O20) | (a) document the out-of-band step and pin the refusal: no code, but an unaudited header edit stays in the loop; (b) an append-only `source.documents` locator that `--policy additive` admits: the declaration becomes part of the reviewed, digest-bound proposal, at the cost of a contract and schema change; (c) declare the whole corpus's digests up front: no code, but the header then names documents no round has read | (b) if the owner wants the loop fully inside `evolve`; otherwise (a). (c) is a host choice, not a GND ruling | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "(b) Add it to evolve (Recommended)"** → an append-only `source.documents` locator admitted by `--policy additive`; UG3 (i) is to be built, subject to its spec gate and UG-Q5. |
| UG-D3 | Fail closed on unchecked spans (MG5-Q3) | (a) leave as deferred: an unattended gate that omits `--document` checks structure only; (b) report counts only, exit unchanged; (c) counts plus an opt-in `--require-documents`-style flag that exits 3 on any unchecked span | (c); (b) if the owner prefers no new flag | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "(c) Counts + strict flag (Recommended)"** → counts always reported, opt-in flag exits 3 on any unchecked span; UG3 (ii) is to be built, subject to its spec gate. |
| UG-D4 | Subtype links carry no `status`/`modality` | (a) keep, as documented: the span, rationale and a reviewed consolidation are the controls; (b) add provenance status to subtype links: a model-schema change with migration and version cost, out of this wave | (a) | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "Approve all as proposed (Recommended)"** → (a). |
| UG-D5 | Host reply shape | (a) documented shape plus a test-only translator, as now (the issue allows "or the skill says the request must cover all of them"); (b) ship a JSON Schema in `gnd-orm-core/references`: pins, sync tests, and a promise nothing in GND reads | (a) | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "Approve all as proposed (Recommended)"** → (a). |
| UG-D6 | Pointing hosts at a duplicate judge | (a) UG4 text: act on a shape match by reusing the existing id, recording the doubt in `open_questions`, or keeping both with a stated reason; (b) also route to `gnd-judge-fact-types`, which is bound to discover evidence files and would need adapting | (a) | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "Approve all as proposed (Recommended)"** → (a). |
| UG-D7 | Extend `--policy additive` to admit `subtype_of` on an existing object type | (a) no: it can change inherited roles, constraints and the reference scheme, so facts may stop being interpretable; consolidation stays a reviewed proposal; (b) admit the narrow case of a subtype with no `inherits_reference` and a supertype with no constraint on a populated fact type: a measured design of its own | (a), as PR 106 and the contract already say | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "Approve all as proposed (Recommended)"** → (a). |
| UG-D8 | Phase 1 | UG1 first, ahead of any code, so dispositions and UG2/UG3 design rest on measured behavior (and so the O20 probe becomes a committed, falsifiable test) | as drafted | **Ruled 2026-11-07 (relayed by the session that put the questions to the owner): "Approve all as proposed (Recommended)"** → as drafted. |

